Source: 551312e3c1b7d5d50566a397bf2c8715134888e3, branch sable-launch-wake, exec3. Base 44e78a7562ba1401b74ab2518aedd14f25d2c4e2.
Oracle-scoped product change: authenticated hook socket discovery plus specific pre-write causes.
The separate Codex trust task and reply-address usability fix are deliberately outside this branch.

Mechanism (source at the gate SHA):
- adapters/hook.rs:378: read documented CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_SOCKET only for Claude SessionStart/Stop, from hook environment; force the capability-authenticated Hook RPC. Unknown stdin fields are stripped. No messaging token is read/forwarded.
- adapters/native.rs:61,86: registration bound to seat, native PID/start, generation and native session; owned Unix socket; in-memory attachment handle is deliberately not persisted identity.
- logic.rs:2343: restore the same validated endpoint on logic restart; :2486 stores only admitted Hook registration, never OSC; :3054 preserves the endpoint when legacy PID-file discovery is absent.
- logic.rs:3202 and native.rs:400: preserve bounded specific pre-write discovery/identity/socket causes. A write/reply ambiguity is still NativeUnknown, without automatic retry or PTY fallback.
- tests/ctl.rs:305: actual app hook shim + MCP bridge, forged OSC rejected, first-contact read/ack/reply, persisted identity, own logic SIGKILL and post-restart native transport. The restart subcase proves receipt/transport only, not post-restart MCP reply.

